(Principles of Computing and Software Systems - Volume 1 \(Page 129 of 700\)) Tj T*
(Chapter 5: Foundations of Discrete Algorithms and Computation) Tj T*
(Section 5.17: Computational Complexity and Memory Bounds) Tj T*
(Theorem 129: Any comparison-based sorting algorithm requires Omega\(n log n\) comparisons in the worst case.) Tj T*
(Proof follows from the binary decision tree height of n! permutations, where log2\(n!\) = n log2\(n\) - O\(n\).) Tj T*
(Exercise 129.1: Verify the asymptotic tight bound for recurrence T\(n\) = 2T\(n/2\) + Theta\(n\).) Tj T*
(Solution: By Case 2 of the Master Theorem, the recurrence evaluates to Theta\(n log n\).) Tj T*
ET
endstream
